---
description: Project rules for AI agents — single source of truth is AGENTS.md
alwaysApply: true
---

Before generating, editing or suggesting any code, read and follow **`AGENTS.md`** at the repository root. It is the single source of truth for scope, architecture, git, dependencies, secrets and costs.

Important: the hooks in `.claude/hooks/` only run inside Claude Code. In Cursor nothing stops you mechanically — **you are the only safety layer**. In particular:

- Never commit, push or merge unless the human asks; never on `main`/`master`.
- Never read or print `.env*`, keys or credential files.
- No new dependencies without the vetting report and approval.
- No paid API/cloud calls and no destructive DB or git operations without explicit approval.

If you cannot access `AGENTS.md`, stop and tell the human.
